    export — and that "Field names in the response are part of the contract; changes go through a versioned endpoint."

  So renaming in place is a breaking change for three consumers, one of which (shipped iOS builds) can't be updated in
  lockstep, and it contradicts the repo's stated versioning policy. The consistency goal is real — [38;5;153mlistOrders[39m already
  uses [38;5;153muser_id[39m — but the in-place rename is the one option the README rules out.
